From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:59:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] usb: dwc2: gadget: Re-arm EP0 on a reset after a
 session event

The USB reset handler re-initialises the device, and re-arms EP0, only
if the device is still "connected". Two events clear that flag while
the host still sees an attached device:
- a VBUS session event: session end, or a session request on VBUS
  rising, both of which call dwc2_hsotg_disconnect();
- a suspend, after which the core sits in L2, clock gated. A host may
  reset a suspended bus without resuming it first, and the reset
  handler left the PHY clock and hclk gated.

The host's next reset then skips the re-initialisation. Enum-done
queues the EP0 setup request into a core outside L0, and
dwc2_hsotg_ep_queue() refuses it:

  dwc2 ...: dwc2_hsotg_enqueue_setup: failed queue (-11)

This repeats on every further reset, and the device never enumerates
until the UDC is unbound and bound again. An Apple iPad 5 (A9) showed it
21-36 times per boot, starting right after the host's first enumeration
and vendor requests.

On a reset:
- leave clock gating if the bus was suspended, as the RESETDET branch
  does for partial power down;
- re-initialise when the B-session is valid and the device was either
  connected or out of L0. Apple's own device controller driver ungates
  its clocks and re-arms EP0 on every reset.

Log the session events and a reset outside L0 (rate-limited; rare), so
that a gadget that stops answering names its cause.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c |  8 ++++++++
 drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c    | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
index 0be67f2..e3bb92d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/core_intr.c
@@ -98,6 +98,10 @@ static void dwc2_handle_otg_intr(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 		gotgctl = dwc2_readl(hsotg, GOTGCTL);
 
 		if (dwc2_is_device_mode(hsotg)) {
+			/* rare, and the cause of a gadget that stops answering mid-session */
+			dev_info_ratelimited(hsotg->dev,
+					     "VBUS session end in L%d (connected %u)\n",
+					     hsotg->lx_state, hsotg->connected);
 			if (hsotg->params.eusb2_disc) {
 				/* Clear the Gate hclk. */
 				pcgctl = dwc2_readl(hsotg, PCGCTL);
@@ -301,6 +305,10 @@ static void dwc2_handle_session_req_intr(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 		hsotg->lx_state);
 
 	if (dwc2_is_device_mode(hsotg)) {
+		if (hsotg->connected)
+			dev_info_ratelimited(hsotg->dev,
+					     "VBUS session request while connected, in L%d: disconnecting\n",
+					     hsotg->lx_state);
 		if (hsotg->lx_state != DWC2_L0) {
 			if (hsotg->in_ppd) {
 				ret = dwc2_exit_partial_power_down(hsotg, 0,
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
index fbc5075..b5afa5e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -3761,6 +3761,7 @@ irq_retry:
 	if (gintsts & (GINTSTS_USBRST | GINTSTS_RESETDET)) {
 		u32 usb_status = dwc2_readl(hsotg, GOTGCTL);
 		u32 connected = hsotg->connected;
+		enum dwc2_lx_state lx = hsotg->lx_state;
 
 		dev_dbg(hsotg->dev, "%s: USBRst\n", __func__);
 		dev_dbg(hsotg->dev, "GNPTXSTS=%08x\n",
@@ -3768,14 +3769,38 @@ irq_retry:
 
 		dwc2_writel(hsotg, GINTSTS_USBRST, GINTSTS);
 
+		/*
+		 * A reset of a suspended bus: no resume came first, so a core
+		 * that entered clock gating on the suspend is still gated.
+		 */
+		if (lx == DWC2_L2 && !hsotg->in_ppd &&
+		    hsotg->params.power_down == DWC2_POWER_DOWN_PARAM_NONE &&
+		    hsotg->bus_suspended && !hsotg->params.no_clock_gating)
+			dwc2_gadget_exit_clock_gating(hsotg, 0);
+
 		/* Report disconnection if it is not already done. */
 		dwc2_hsotg_disconnect(hsotg);
 
 		/* Reset device address to zero */
 		dwc2_clear_bit(hsotg, DCFG, DCFG_DEVADDR_MASK);
 
-		if (usb_status & GOTGCTL_BSESVLD && connected)
+		/*
+		 * The host resets an attached device.  A device that a session
+		 * event (VBUS session end or request) or a suspend took out of
+		 * L0 is no longer "connected", yet the host never saw it go:
+		 * without the re-initialisation the EP0 setup request that
+		 * enum-done queues is refused outside L0 (-EAGAIN) on this and
+		 * every later reset, until the UDC is rebound.  Re-arm it as
+		 * for a connected device, as Apple's device controller driver
+		 * does on every reset.
+		 */
+		if (usb_status & GOTGCTL_BSESVLD && (connected || lx != DWC2_L0))
 			dwc2_hsotg_core_init_disconnected(hsotg, true);
+		if (lx != DWC2_L0)
+			dev_info_ratelimited(hsotg->dev,
+					     "USB reset in L%d (connected %u, B-session %s): EP0 re-armed\n",
+					     lx, connected,
+					     usb_status & GOTGCTL_BSESVLD ? "valid" : "invalid");
 	}
 
 	if (gintsts & GINTSTS_ENUMDONE) {
